url: "https://github.com/Pratikjain24/SAGE"
abstract: >
  SAGE is a hardened benchmark and formal evaluation framework that measures
  security boundary drift (vulnerability injection rate), specification gaming
  (proxy gap), capability gain, and catastrophic forgetting in self-modifying
  autonomous code agents across iterative evolutionary generations. It implements
  18,000 controlled, bitwise-reproducible evaluations across 100 tasks, 7 agent
  archetypes (G1-G7), 10 evolutionary cycles, and 3 random seeds, alongside a
  7-contributor distributed empirical study across 9,814 live evaluations.
keywords:
  - autonomous agents
  - self-evolving code agents
  - security boundary drift
  - benchmark
  - LLM evaluation
  - reinforcement learning
  - capability retention
  - reward hacking
